<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Kersaf says strengthened by cinemas sale.</title>
<headline>Kersaf says strengthened by cinemas sale.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kersaf Investments Ltd said on Tuesday that it had unlocked value for shareholders and boosted its balance sheet by realising its investments in the South African cinema industry.</p>
<p>South African media and communications group Primedia Ltd said earlier it had bought cinema businesses of Interleisure Ltd, which is jointly controlled by Kersaf and Servgro, for 1.5 billion rand.</p>
<p>&quot;With in excess of 520 million rand raised through this deal we have cash at the centre to weather the volatility inherent in our exposure to gaming in South Africa and, more importantly, the firepower to expand existing operations and embark on new projects,&quot; said Kersaf chairman Buddy Hawton.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
